<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p><h1 class="research-title">46 BCE</h1><p class="ref-lede">46 BCE in world history: 5 events, 4 deaths and 1 state that came to an end. 177 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/54-bce">54 BCE</a><a href="/years/51-bce">51 BCE</a><a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a><a href="/years/48-bce">48 BCE</a><a href="/years/46-bce" aria-current="page">46 BCE</a><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a><a href="/years/43-bce">43 BCE</a><a href="/years/42-bce">42 BCE</a><a href="/years/31-bce">31 BCE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-4">4 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Caesar narrowly escapes defeat at the Battle of Ruspina</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s outnumbered army was surrounded by Republican forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus">Titus Labienus</a>. Caesar fought his way back to camp, surviving to defeat his enemies at Thapsus three months later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thapsus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-thapsus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-6">6 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar defeats Metellus Scipio at the Battle of Thapsus</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Thapsus, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> defeated the Pompeian forces of Metellus Scipio and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I of Numidia</a>. The victory destroyed the republican cause in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-younger">Cato the Younger</a>, Scipio and Juba took their own lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thapsus">Battle of Thapsus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-younger">Cato the Younger</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-26">26 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar dedicates the Temple of Venus Genetrix</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the celebrations of his triumphs, Caesar dedicated a temple to Venus Genetrix, the mythical ancestress of his family, in his new forum. It proclaimed his divine lineage and unrivalled power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
